{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'wc -l src/hivemind/release.py scripts/release_build.py tests/test_release.py docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_{check,mutants}.py poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23e/results.json; tail -3 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md'","aggregated_output":"     487 src/hivemind/release.py\n     123 scripts/release_build.py\n     715 tests/test_release.py\n     266 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py\n      95 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_mutants.py\n   44681 poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23e/results.json\n   46367 total\n| 39 | 11-05 | 第 3 步：做进正式系统（设计四张表，Codex 审 3 轮：第 1 轮 4 条严重、第 2 轮 2 条严重，都改；第 3 轮无严重问题） | 建成 `baseline.run` + poc-v116 + baseline-v3 提示词文件；$0 核对：44 份请求和验证时逐字节相同，3 次存下的回答走正式代码写出的记录完全一样，第一天判断正好判这些题，网页从开始跟踪那天可见；新测试 12 条、6 个弄坏版本都抓出、全套 272 条通过；设计页和 PRD 00/03/04/05/06 更新，`docs/check.py` 通过 | 交 Alex：要不要跑 14 天三遍完整验收（约 5 美元） |\n| 40 | 11-05 | Alex：\"跑验收\"。14 天三遍完整验收：poc-v116（开始跟踪时读财报）三遍、当天重跑 poc-v108 三遍作对照，冻结尺子打分（事先锁定 `acceptance-design.md`）；电脑中途在电池上睡了约 5 小时，6 遍被暂停，插电后自己接着跑完 | **全过**：v10、v12 各 3/3（对照从没判过）；合计 53 对 45（满分 57，+8）；唯一少两次的 v17（0/3 对 2/3）两人都认定不是起点数：同一份抽取请求，新配置两遍碰巧留下\"中国份额归零\"那句，对照没留；约 4.79 美元 | 交 Alex：poc-v116 是否成为默认 |\n| 41 | 11-05 | Alex：\"都做\"（poc-v116 设成默认；提交代码、开 PR）。默认配置改成 poc-v116，默认的条目数据库换成带财报网页原文的那一份（旧的没有原文，新默认会在它上面拒跑）；测试按用户的用法补上：不给种子题就拒绝，给了就先读财报再跑第一天 | 测试全过，5 个弄坏的版本都抓出；配置的设置和验收三遍记下的校验码一致（只改了配置里的注释）；花钱前的检查脚本在新配置的运行数据上照常跑完，但不复查读财报那一步的引用检查（记为未补的缺口）；D366 | 提交、开 PR；下一类问题等 Alex |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md && rg -n '\"'^#|revision 11'\"' RELEASE-BUILD.md\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# \"Forecast unavailable\" release, slice 1: built and checked at $0 (2026-11-23)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Result.** Slice 1 is built to `RELEASE-BUILD.md`:\n     4\t- revision 10 was ready per council 74j, after ten review rounds;\n     5\t- revision 11 records what councils 75 to 75d required of the build.\n     6\t\n     7\tIt passes its tests, its mutants and the $0 release check on four stored stores. Nothing is committed, published or deployed. The POC\n     8\tis unchanged; no POC code imports the release module.\n     9\t\n    10\t- Code: `src/hivemind/release.py`, `scripts/release_build.py`, `tests/test_release.py`.\n    11\t- Check: `release_check.py`; mutants: `release_mutants.py` (both in this folder).\n    12\t- Output: `poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23e/`. The runs `release-check-2026-11-23/` to `-23d/` predate later fixes and are kept for\n    13\t  the record. Their counts and bytes are the same; their seconds differ by run.\n    14\t\n    15\t## 1. Council 75's findings, and what changed\n    16\t\n    17\tCouncil 75 (`codex-r75.md`) reproduced the four packages' counts and both refusals of the substituted forecast. It did not accept the\n    18\tslice. Its findings and the fixes:\n    19\t\n    20\t| Finding | Fix | Proof |\n    21\t|---|---|---|\n    22\t| A key written after the bound could reclassify an earlier package (the key lookup ignored its `seq`) | the key counts only when visible at the bound | test 22; mutant \"key read without its day\" |\n    23\t| Ten text fields accepted null, which revision 10 forbids | strings only | test 23; mutant \"null accepted as text\" |\n    24\t| `check` read the data file three times: it could hash one version and certify another | one read through one folder handle; hash and parse the same bytes; the command reports that data | structural (`check_package`) |\n    25\t| A path holding `%` could make SQLite open a different file from the one named | `release.store_path` refuses `%`, `?`, `#` | test 24; mutant \"store-path refusal removed\" |\n    26\t| Test 14's marker case supplied the very line its mutant removes | the instrumentation no longer touches the line that drops the staging path | test 14; mutant caught |\n    27\t| Test 13 damaged two things | the package copy keeps `e2` with no source, which is what a checker that drops missing items expects | test 13; mutant \"inner join\" caught |\n    28\t| Tests 1, 2 and 9 lacked decisive assertions | test 25 proves the writer's own refusal; test 2 checks all five labels in `v1`'s own fields; test 9 names each refusal's reason | mutants caught |\n    29\t| The mutant runner counted any non-zero exit | it stops on a failing control, and counts a catch only with a failing test and no setup or collection error | run below |\n    30\t| My first result overstated the closing check, the diagnostic search and the dated check, and the script never failed | corrected below; the script now fails on any missed acceptance item or budget | this run |\n    31\t\n    32\t**Council 75b** (`codex-r75b.md`) confirmed the fixes above and found four more gaps, now fixed:\n    33\t\n    34\t| Finding | Fix | Proof |\n    35\t|---|---|---|\n    36\t| The store-path check returned the original path, which the opener resolved again | `store_path` returns the resolved path, and the opener is given that | test 24 (a symbolic link); mutant \"store path returned unresolved\" |\n    37\t| A named pipe in a package would make `check` hang instead of refusing | files are opened without waiting (`O_NONBLOCK`), then refused by type | test 15, through the command with a 30 s bound; mutant \"pipe opened blocking\" |\n    38\t| The check script could pass with a required example missing | the three examples are a fixed list; a missing one fails the script | this run |\n    39\t| No test reordered records, and the runner credited a failure of a test's own scratch edit | test 10 reorders questions and evidence; scratch edits fail with \"scratch anchor\", which the runner does not count | mutant \"check_origins accepting another order\" |\n    40\t\n    41\tIt also asked that test 23 cover all ten text fields (now one case per field) and that test 2 check every question's own fields for\n    42\tthe labels (done).\n    43\t\n    44\t**Council 75c** (`codex-r75c.md`) found no off-list field or mismatched value, and judged every code finding of 75 and 75b closed. It\n    45\tfound three verification gaps, now fixed:\n    46\t\n    47\t| Finding | Fix | Proof |\n    48\t|---|---|---|\n    49\t| The runner read only pytest's short line, which can omit the \"scratch anchor\" message | each failure's full message is read from pytest's XML report | this run |\n    50\t| Test 2 skipped evidence fields; test 21 did not check that the whole report is printed | test 2 allows a `v1` label only in the fixture's known genuine source text; test 21 parses the printed report | mutants \"a number label written into another question's evidence\", \"report not printed\" |\n    51\t| The check script accepted an example id whose text had changed | superseded by council 75d's rule below | this run |\n    52\t\n    53\t**Council 75d** (`codex-r75d.md`) again found no off-list field or mismatched value. Its three findings had one mechanism:\n    54\t- test 2 took its \"genuine\" text from the export under test;\n    55\t- test 21 accepted a partial report;\n    56\t- the acceptance script's \"$390 billion\" also matches the system's own forecast, and a stale-hash refusal satisfied a check meant\n    57\t  for another reason.\n    58\t\n    59\t**One structural rule now holds** (AGENTS §1): every acceptance assertion compares against fixed expected values written down before\n    60\tthe run, never values taken from the output under test, and every refusal check matches its exact reason:\n    61\t- test 2 allows a label only in the fixture's own two constant texts;\n    62\t- tests 11 and 21 require the report's exact key set and fixed values;\n    63\t- the script compares each example's full summary and quote with the stored text written into it (old-1, 2026-11-23), and each\n    64\t  refusal with its exact message;\n    65\t- mutant \"report missing a field\" proves the key-set check.\n    66\t\n    67\t**No regression.**\n    68\t- The release tests: 36 pass. The full suite passes: 425 tests, the frozen-ruler guards included.\n    69\t- Mutants: 31 of 32 are caught by failing tests, each judged from its full failure message (a failure of the test's own scratch edit\n    70\t  does not count), with no setup errors.\n    71\t- **The 32nd, the canonical-day check removed, is equivalent on this repository's Python 3.10.10,** whose `date.fromisoformat` already\n    72\t  refuses `20260825`. Under Python 3.13, on a temporary copy of `old-1` with one later completed day:\n    73\t  - the real code refuses `20260825`;\n    74\t  - the mutant exports `v8` with 1,284 pieces of evidence through 2026-09-20 into a package dated 2026-08-25, where the right package\n    75\t    holds 621.\n    76\t\n    77\t## 2. The $0 release check (design §7)\n    78\t\n    79\t| Store | Bound | Number / event / Yes-No | Evidence | Fields compared | Data bytes (library) | Seconds (library) |\n    80\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n    81\t| old-1 | 2026-09-20 | 19 / 28 / 0 | 8,251 | 91,055 | 5,788,634 (14,478,536) | 8.25 (6.52) |\n    82\t| old-2 | 2026-09-20 | 17 / 26 / 0 | 6,306 | 69,636 | 4,427,609 (11,893,701) | 6.24 (4.99) |\n    83\t| old-3 | 2026-09-20 | 18 / 31 / 0 | 6,659 | 73,559 | 4,685,247 (12,375,915) | 6.70 (5.38) |\n    84\t| served | 2026-08-28 | 13 / 55 / 0 | 6,461 | 71,524 | 4,612,321 (12,145,774) | 4.33 (3.40) |\n    85\t\n    86\t- **Every package passed its origin check:** every field compared with its stored source at the bound.\n    87\t- **No number question is unresolved** in these stores.\n    88\t- **Budgets met:**\n    89\t  - the bytes are 0.37–0.40 of the existing library's;\n    90\t  - the seconds are 1.25–1.27 times the library's, against a budget of 3 times and 120 s.\n    91\t- **How the evidence is counted.** The count includes each piece once per question that holds it. Every piece has exactly one source\n    92\t  row (`old-1`: 5,390 rows for 5,390 pieces).\n    93\t- **The script exits non-zero on any missed acceptance item** (each example, refusal, leak, control and closing check named in it) or\n    94\t  budget; this run ended \"every acceptance item and budget met\".\n    95\t\n    96\t**The decisive acceptance case** (council 74, `old-1`):\n    97\t- **Kept, each equal to the store and to its full text written into the script before the run:**\n    98\t  - Morningstar's $361 billion (`e2295`, under `v8`);\n    99\t  - the genuine \"Bullish confirmation\" quote (`e1865`, under `v4`, `v5`, `v8`);\n   100\t  - the analysts' \"$390 billion\" (`e3597`, under `v4`, `v5`).\n   101\t- **The system's own forecast** (`j1580` implied outcome, \"About $390 billion: …\"):\n   102\t  - substituted into `e2295`'s summary, it is refused with exactly \"question v8.evidence e2295.one_line: differs from the store\";\n   103\t  - added to the manifest, it is refused with exactly \"the manifest: keys off the allow-list ['note'], missing []\".\n   104\t\n   105\t**The other checks:**\n   106\t- **`old-1/v8`:** class `number`, marked \"Forecast unavailable\". Its 1,284 pieces of evidence are the same ids as `service.evidence` at\n   107\t  the bound.\n   108\t- **The known Yes/No leaks at their own days.**\n   109\t  - `old-3/v36` at 2026-08-25 (judgement 799) and `old-1/v10` at 2026-08-28 (judgement 865) are the latest judgements there.\n   110\t  - Both keep \"Yes\".\n   111\t  - The full explanation and reason texts are absent.\n   112\t  - So are the judgements' own phrases: \"around $1 trillion\", \"rung 4\", \"at rung\" and \"capex at rung\" occur in no field.\n   113\t- **Control:** event `old-1/v3` keeps \"Yes\" and its evidence, equal to the store.\n   114\t- **Closing,** on a copy of `old-1` with a closing switch for `v8`, \"due 2026-09-20, frozen on 2026-09-20 at rung 2 Bullish\":\n   115\t  - `bundle.view_bundle` exposes it;\n   116\t  - the package shows `open: false`;\n   117\t  - the reason appears nowhere.\n   118\t  - The word \"Bullish\" does occur inside six `v8` fields: five source titles and the genuine `e1865` quote. That is source wording,\n   119\t    which the design keeps.\n   120\t\n   121\t## 3. The diagnostic search, every hit read\n   122\t\n   123\tThe search covered every decoded string of each package, ids, classes, the marker and the manifest included. For each question it\n   124\ttook every stored string the package must not hold:\n   125\t- rung labels of number questions;\n   126\t- the rung conditions of every question;\n   127\t- judgement reasons, explanations, implied outcomes and references, where the store has those columns (the served ledger lacks the\n   128\t  last two);\n   129\t- every switch reason, \"created\" included.\n   130\t\n   131\t| Store | Stored strings judged | Package strings | Hits |\n   132\t|---|---|---|---|\n   133\t| old-1 | 6,670 | 91,012 | 1,378: \"created\" 987, \"Bullish\" 391 |\n   134\t| old-2 | 6,677 | 69,597 | 771: \"created\" 516, \"Bullish\" 255 |\n   135\t| old-3 | 7,045 | 73,514 | 1,613: \"created\" 1,176, labels 437 (\"Bullish\", \"High\", \"Low\", \"Bearish\", \"Middle\") |\n   136\t| served | 2,149 | 71,460 | 1,794: \"created\" 1,632, \"Bullish\" 162 |\n   137\t\n   138\t- **No condition, reason, explanation, implied outcome, reference or closing reason is found anywhere.**\n   139\t- **The label hits are 257 package fields holding 32 distinct texts, all read.** Every one is source wording:\n   140\t  - headlines: \"Jensen Huang's Bullish Call …\", \"Stock Traded Lower\", \"Earnings Call Highlights\", \"Lows Not Seen Since 2019\",\n   141\t    \"Sky-High P/E\", \"That Bearish Bet\";\n   142\t  - the memory term \"High Bandwidth Memory\";\n   143\t  - the analyst quote \"Bullish confirmation would require …\".\n   144\t- **The \"created\" hits fall in 33 distinct texts, all containing the ordinary word.** It is every question's creation reason and\n   145\t  carries no forecast.\n   146\t\n   147\t## 4. Not shown, and still open\n   148\t\n   149\t- **The reader's screen** (slice 2, D756's screen check) is not built. The release page must read only this package, with no live\n   150\t  fetch and no idea submission, and needs a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen.\n   151\t- **The idea path in the release:** deferred (council 74); its acceptance is pending.\n   152\t- **The recorded disagreement on evidence summaries** (`RELEASE-BUILD.md` §8) stands.\n   153\t- **`store.open_read_only` puts a path into a SQLite URI unescaped.** That is shared POC code; the release refuses such paths\n   154\t  rather than changing it.\n1:# \"Forecast unavailable\" release: build design for slice 1 (the exporter and the checked package)\n3:**Status: revision 11. Built** (`src/hivemind/release.py`, `scripts/release_build.py`, `tests/test_release.py`; result in\n4:`RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md`). Revision 10 was ready per council 74j; revision 11 records the changes council 75 required of the build.\n90:## 0. Scope\n110:## 1. What is built\n249:## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\n286:## 3. Value × reader\n315:## 4. New path × old checks\n329:## 5. Prior decisions\n341:## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\n444:## 7. The $0 release check (stored stores, read-only)\n480:## 8. A disclosed property, not built: evidence summaries keep extraction's wording\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && for f in codex-r75*.md; do echo \"$f\"; nl -ba \"$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && for f in codex-r75*.md; do echo \"$f\"; nl -ba \"$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"codex-r75.md\n     1\t**Verdict: slice 1 is not accepted.** All four saved packages passed my read-only comparison with their stores. I also reproduced both refusals of the substituted $390 billion forecast. The release still accepts a value revision 10 forbids, and I reproduced a historical case where the exporter and checker agree on an answer that should have been withheld. [Saved acceptance results:10079](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23/results.json:10079)\n     2\t\n     3\t### 1. Design and leaks\n     4\t\n     5\t| Finding | Evidence and consequence |\n     6\t|---|---|\n     7\t| **A later classification can expose an earlier forecast.** | In memory, an August 24 question initially exported “Forecast unavailable.” After adding an event key dated August 25, the **same August 24 export** showed “Above the estimate,” and the origin check passed. Both paths use a key lookup that ignores its sequence. The normal writer creates the key with the question, and I found zero sequence mismatches in the four stores. The exposure applies to a snapshot that breaks that convention. [Key lookup:81](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:81) · [Origin check:289](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:289) · [Writer:42](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:42) |\n     8\t| **Ten required text fields accept `null`.** | Revision 10 requires strings for all six evidence text fields and all four source fields. On an in-memory copy of `old-1`, a visible evidence record with a null summary passed both export and origin checking. This is a package-contract failure. I found no such null in the four saved packages. [Design:138](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:138) · [Type check:170](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:170) · [Affected fields:210](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:210) |\n     9\t| **`check` can verify different bytes from the ones it hashes or reports.** | It checks file type by pathname, reads the data for its hash, then reopens it for parsing. The command opens it a third time for the report. If an existing package changes during verification, the hash, origin comparison, and reported date can describe different contents. The four stored packages were stable. [Package reads:400](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:400) · [Report read:86](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/release_build.py:86) |\n    10\t| **Both commands can open a different database from the path named in the report.** | The release passes paths to an opener that inserts the literal filename into a SQLite URI without escaping it. I verified that SQLite decodes `%2D` in a directory name to `-`. If both literal paths exist, the filesystem check can inspect one database while export and origin checking read the other. The four recorded input paths do not have this ambiguity. [Command:51](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/release_build.py:51) · [Filesystem check:40](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/live_lock.py:40) · [SQLite open:229](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:229) |\n    11\t\n    12\tThere are also command and diagnostic departures with no observed forecast exposure. On a report-write failure, `check` prints only counts, so the user loses the date, unresolved list, size, and timings that revision 10 says it prints. Timings use the adjustable wall clock. An export-side missing-item error omits the evidence ID, and a changed summary is reported by list position instead of evidence ID. The direct visibility test and the separate required item lookup implement the specified selection and missing-item refusal on a stable snapshot. [Command contract:213](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:213) · [Printed result:98](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/release_build.py:98) · [Timer:48](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/release_build.py:48) · [Item error:116](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:116) · [Observed summary error:10104](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23/results.json:10104)\n    13\t\n    14\t### 2. Tests and mutants\n    15\t\n    16\tThe recorded full-suite run did pass 412 tests. I reviewed all 23 release tests. Several assertions can pass after the behavior they claim to protect has been removed. [Suite output:6](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/tasks/bt1qa93h2.output:6)\n    17\t\n    18\t- **The staging-ownership test supplies the behavior it claims to prove.** Its instrumentation inserts `staged = None` itself. The mutant removes the exact text the instrumentation needs to find, so setup can fail before the marker is created. This leaves the claimed marker-survival proof vacuous against its designated mutant. [Test:548](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:548) · [Edit precondition:468](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:468) · [Mutant:38](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_mutants.py:38)\n    19\t- **The missing-item test damages two things.** It removes the source and the entire `e2` record. A checker that silently skips a missing source still expects `e2` with an empty source list, so it refuses this package for an independent reason. The mutant fails the expected-message assertion, but the design explicitly requires a pair the faulty checker *accepts*. [Test:345](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:345) · [Checker:245](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:245) · [Design:365](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:365)\n    20\t- **Three other protections lack a decisive assertion.** Test 1 calls `check_export` again after export, so it cannot detect removal of the writer’s self-check. Test 2 omits the selected label “Bullish” and the label “Bearish” from its forbidden list. Test 9 changes a stored summary and accepts any refusal, so origin checking still makes it pass if hash verification is removed. [Test 1:180](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:180) · [Test 2:191](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:191) · [Test 9:280](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:280)\n    21\t- **“21 of 22 caught” counts failing processes.** The scratch copies exclude bytecode and use their own source path. The runner nevertheless continues after a failed control and counts every nonzero pytest exit, including setup errors. Its “sets” mutant only deduplicates questions while preserving order. The date exception is supported independently: on Python 3.13 I reproduced 621 pieces for August 25 and 1,284 through September 20 with the compact-date mutant. [Mutant edits:25](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_mutants.py:25) · [Environment and counting:44](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_mutants.py:44) · [Date result:16](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:16)\n    22\t\n    23\t### 3. The $0 result\n    24\t\n    25\tI reproduced the reported class, evidence, source, and field-comparison counts for all four default packages. The byte and time ratios follow from the saved numbers. The closing switch also worked: `v8` was closed and its full closing reason was absent. Three claims exceed what the check established. [Store results:3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23/results.json:3) · [Closing result:10140](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23/results.json:10140)\n    26\t\n    27\t- **“Bullish” appears in six `v8` fields in the closing package.** Five are source titles and one is the genuine `e1865` quote. The script tested whole-field equality. The report claimed absence from every field. These six occurrences are permitted source wording. [Comparison:226](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:226) · [Claim:60](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:60) · [Six field locations:140](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23/results.json:140)\n    28\t- **The diagnostic search was incomplete.** Across the four packages it skipped 28,170 decoded data strings plus all 16 manifest strings. It also skipped event conditions and the stored switch reason `created`, which occurs in 81 actual package fields. Revision 10 calls for reading every hit. The report records a sample of 14 out of 1,245 reported matches. [Field selection:49](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:49) · [Stored-string selection:76](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:76) · [Requirement:451](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:451) · [Sample:81](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:81)\n    29\t- **The dated check never tests j865’s selected-band phrase.** It searches for the full explanation and for j799’s “around $1 trillion.” A shortened copy containing only j865’s “rung 4” would escape that check. I searched the saved August 28 data separately and found zero occurrences of “rung 4.” The script also records failed acceptance comparisons and exceeded budgets as values in JSON without making them fail the command. [Required dated check:445](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:445) · [Actual comparison:190](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:190) · [Budget handling:143](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:143) · [Command completion:227](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:227)\n    30\t\n    31\tThe four saved packages support the narrower conclusion that their forecasts were withheld and their permitted content matched the named stores. The historical classification case, accepted nulls, and verification gaps prevent accepting slice 1 as specified.codex-r75b.md\n     1\t**Verdict: slice 1 is not accepted.** All four saved packages matched their stores. The August 24 buyback question now says “Forecast unavailable,” and the August 25 package shows “Above the estimate.” Two command defects and two gaps in the acceptance checks remain. [Date correction](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:87) · [Two-day test](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:610)\n     2\t\n     3\t### Findings that block acceptance\n     4\t\n     5\t| Finding | Evidence and consequence |\n     6\t|---|---|\n     7\t| **Both commands can still verify against the wrong database if a store symlink changes.** | The release checks the characters in the resolved path, then returns the original path. The opener resolves it a second time. If the link changes between those operations, the path used by SQLite can differ from the one that passed the check. Export and verification can then agree with each other while reading the wrong store. The fix covers stable paths, including the four saved inputs. Test 24 exercises a fixed directory only. [Release path check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:405) · [Second resolution](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/live_lock.py:42) · [SQLite open](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:228) · [Test 24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:630) |\n     8\t| **The revised package reader can hang indefinitely on a file it promises to refuse.** | It opens each entry for blocking reads before checking its type. For a named pipe with no writer, the open waits and the regular-file check is never reached. This is a new failure in `check`. The existing test covers a symbolic link. [Open and type check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:414) · [Regular-file requirement](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:192) · [File test](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:363) |\n     9\t| **The acceptance script can pass with a required example missing.** | It builds the list of examples from whichever requested IDs the database returns, then checks only that list. I replayed its final decision in memory against the saved results. Removing `e1865` or `e3597`, one at a time, produced zero failures in both cases. All three examples were present in the actual run. The report’s claim that *any* missed item fails the command is too broad. [Selection](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:158) · [Pass decision](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:234) · [Report claim](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:57) |\n    10\t| **The round-75 finding about order remains open.** | The production checker compares ordered lists. The test labeled “comparing sets” still removes duplicate question IDs while preserving their order. Test 10 adds duplicates and never swaps two distinct entries. Its success therefore gives no evidence that the suite catches a checker that accepts reordered records. The runner now stops on a failed control, but it still credits any failed test body, including a scratch-edit assertion, without checking which assertion failed. [Production comparison](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:293) · [Mutant](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_mutants.py:25) · [Test 10](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:315) · [Scratch assertion](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:471) · [Runner verdict](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_mutants.py:77) |\n    11\t\n    12\t### Other round-75 findings\n    13\t\n    14\t- **Historical classification and required text are fixed in code.** I checked both buyback dates and independently tried `null` in each of the ten required evidence and source fields. All ten were refused. Test 23 itself exercises only the summary, so it would still pass if validation disappeared from the four source fields. [Text validation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:212) · [Source validation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:217) · [Test 23](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:618)\n    15\t- **The hash, parser, and command report now use the same data.** Both commands print the full report before attempting to write it and use monotonic timing. Missing-source and changed-summary errors now identify the evidence. Test 9 requires the hash-specific refusal. [Package read](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:455) · [Report output](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/release_build.py:29) · [Check timing and data](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/release_build.py:88) · [Missing source](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:122) · [Test 9](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:283)\n    16\t- **The staging-marker, missing-item, and writer self-check tests now distinguish the intended failures.** Test 2 also checks all five forecast labels, although only within `v1`. A label copied into another question would escape that assertion. [Marker survival](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:551) · [Missing-item pair](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:356) · [Writer self-check pair](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:662) · [Label assertion](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:198)\n    17\t\n    18\t### What the saved run establishes\n    19\t\n    20\tI reproduced all four packages’ comparison counts and byte sizes, plus both refusals of the substituted `$390 billion` forecast. The saved timings meet the stated budgets. The dated checks now include “rung 4.” The closing package shows `v8` closed, omits its closing reason, and retains the six genuine source occurrences of “Bullish.” The recorded full suite passed 416 tests. [Store results](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23b/results.json:3) · [Both refusals](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23b/results.json:44592) · [Dated checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23b/results.json:44602) · [Closing check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23b/results.json:44638) · [Suite result](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/tasks/bi89r1zvy.output:3)\n    21\t\n    22\tOne diagnostic count needs correction. The forecast-label matches occupy **257 package fields containing 32 distinct texts**. Every match was in a source title or quote. The report calls these “32 distinct places.” I found no off-list value or value unequal to its store in the four reviewed packages. [Diagnostic records](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23b/results.json:27) · [Report wording](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:102)codex-r75c.md\n     1\t**Verdict: slice 1 is not accepted.** I rechecked all four saved packages against their stores and found no off-list field or mismatched value. The production checker also refused both copies containing the substituted `$390 billion` forecast. Three verification gaps remain. [Saved refusals and unchanged control, results.json:44594](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23c/results.json:44594)\n     2\t\n     3\t1. **The mutant runner can still credit a failed test setup as a catch.** It looks for `scratch anchor` only in pytest’s short `FAILED` line. I reproduced an anchor-only failure under test 12’s name. The traceback contained `scratch anchor`, but the short line contained only the test name. The runner counted that line as a catch. This leaves the report’s claim that 28 catches exclude scratch-edit failures unverified. [release_mutants.py:82](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_mutants.py:82) · [test_release.py:488](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:488) · [RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:46](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:46)\n     4\t\n     5\t2. **Two tests still pass when the protection they name is removed.** I changed `v6`’s evidence summary to `Bullish` in memory. Test 2 passed because its cross-question label check skips every evidence field. The production checker correctly refused `question v6.evidence e5.one_line`. Test 21 likewise checks only for `passes` and the write error. Removing the line that prints the full report leaves both assertions satisfied. [test_release.py:198](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:198) · [test_release.py:609](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:609) · [release_build.py:31](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/release_build.py:31)\n     6\t\n     7\t3. **The acceptance script can lose the decisive quote and still pass.** A missing example ID now fails. An ID whose text no longer contains the required example still passes if the package matches the store. In memory, I replaced `e3597`’s analyst `$390 billion` text with `e2295`’s `$361 billion` text on both sides. The script marked `e3597` present and equal, and its final decision returned zero failures. The genuine quote was present in the saved run. [Required control, RELEASE-BUILD.md:456](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:456) · [release_check.py:163](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:163) · [release_check.py:238](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:238)\n     8\t\n     9\tThe other round-75 and 75b findings are closed for the reviewed snapshots. The fixes cover historical classification, all ten required text fields, resolved store paths, nonblocking pipe refusal, hashing and parsing the same bytes, and ordered comparisons. The revised staging-marker, missing-item, writer-self-check and hash tests distinguish their intended failures. [release.py:87](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:87) · [release.py:410](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:410) · [release.py:417](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:417) · [release.py:458](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:458) · [test_release.py:286](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:286) · [test_release.py:328](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:328) · [test_release.py:367](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:367) · [test_release.py:568](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:568) · [test_release.py:639](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:639) · [test_release.py:701](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:701)\n    10\t\n    11\t**The report also quotes the preceding run’s timings.** The new release/library seconds are `8.55/6.69`, `6.76/5.09`, `6.90/5.46`, and `4.48/3.51` in table order. The actual range is **1.26–1.33×**. All four still meet both budgets. The package counts, byte sizes, dated answers, closing result, and 257 label-matching fields holding 32 distinct texts checked out. The subsequent full-suite run passed 425 tests. [Report table:57](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:57) · [old-1:19](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23c/results.json:19) · [old-2:11071](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23c/results.json:11071) · [old-3:17267](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23c/results.json:17267) · [served:30199](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23c/results.json:30199) · [Full-suite output:2](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/tasks/buduqedk6.output:2)codex-r75d.md\n     1\t**Verdict — slice 1 is not accepted.** I rechecked all four saved packages against their stores and found no off-list field or mismatched value. The production checker also refused both copies containing the substituted `$390 billion` forecast for the expected reasons. Three verification gaps remain. [results.json:44597](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23d/results.json:44597)\n     2\t\n     3\t1. **Test 2 still accepts a forecast label in an evidence summary.** I replaced `e6`’s summary with the single word `Bullish` in memory. Test 2 passed. It takes the text it considers genuine from `e6` in the export under test, so changing the summary also changes the expected answer. The production checker correctly refused `question v5.evidence e6.one_line`. The test needs to compare each permitted occurrence with the fixture’s original text at that location. [Fixture, test_release.py:107](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:107) · [Assertion, test_release.py:203](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:203)\n     4\t\n     5\t2. **Test 21 still accepts an incomplete printed report.** I replayed its assertions with a report containing only the date, one comparison count and `export_seconds`. It passed with both store paths, the unresolved list, byte size and check time missing. The command currently prints the full report, and the new mutant proves that removing *all* report output is caught. The test needs to check the complete set of required fields. [Test, test_release.py:610](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:610) · [Report contents, RELEASE-BUILD.md:238](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:238) · [Command, release_build.py:100](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/release_build.py:100)\n     6\t\n     7\t3. **The decisive acceptance check can pass after the genuine analyst quote is gone.** In memory, I replaced `e3597`’s quote in both the stored record and its package copies with the system’s own `j1580` forecast. The script marked the quote present, equal to the store and holding its own wording. It returned zero failures because both texts contain `$390 billion`. The refusal checks have a related gap. A stale-hash refusal also satisfied the check that specifically requires the substituted summary to fail comparison with its store. The acceptance case needs wording that distinguishes the analyst quote and the specific reason for each refusal. [Required case, RELEASE-BUILD.md:453](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:453) · [Wording check, release_check.py:162](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:162) · [Pass decision, release_check.py:240](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:240)\n     8\t\n     9\tThe other findings from rounds 75, 75b and 75c are closed for the reviewed snapshots. Those fixes cover historical classification, all ten required text fields, resolved store paths, nonblocking pipe refusal, hashing and parsing the same bytes, ordered records, and the staging, missing-item and writer self-check tests. The mutant runner now checks the full XML failure text for a failed scratch edit. [release.py:87](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:87) · [release.py:458](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:458) · [test_release.py:329](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:329) · [test_release.py:642](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:642) · [release_mutants.py:86](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_mutants.py:86)\n    10\t\n    11\t**The rewritten report’s measurements hold.** I reproduced all four comparison counts and byte sizes, both forecast refusals, and the 257 label-matching fields containing 32 distinct texts. The saved timings support the reported 1.24–1.26× range. The recorded runs show 36 release tests passed, 30 of 31 mutants caught and 425 full-suite tests passed. The overstatements are that the two test gaps are closed and that every missed acceptance item makes the script fail. [Report claims, RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:49](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:49) · [Acceptance claim, RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:79](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:79) · [Full-suite output:2](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/tasks/bwx9cysnh.output:2)codex-r75e.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
