{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'release|Slice 1|slice 1' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | head -12; sed -n '240,252p' src/hivemind/views/store.py; rg -n 'pytest' pyproject.toml\"","aggregated_output":"91:**Measurement correction (2026-11-05):** Alex clarified that a gold-worthy topic already in the supplied library should not open again; an absent worthy topic should open. The earlier simple-A claim of a \"missed\" new topic was not scored against that rule and is withdrawn as a correctness conclusion. In the actual experiment, a Kyber topic was shown and passing follows Alex's topic-level rule; whether its exact release question captures the shipping milestone remains unverified. The experimental pre-article snapshots differ from the replay's day-start snapshots; 9 of 10 inspected examples differ. The current uncommitted replay default does not build a cold-start library; committed main HEAD still uses the old seed and startup filing path. Historical lexical coverage has a confirmed unrelated-topic match. The frozen gold and past scores remain unchanged. Audit: `../hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-parallel-refinement/measurement-context-scrub-2026-11-05.zh.md`.\n93:**Simple new-question diagnostic (2026-11-05):** At Alex's direction, an isolated prompt returned new questions plus article evidence without asking for product database fields. Four previously seen real dev articles each ran once: three returned one candidate, one returned none, all four quotes matched their source, and the gold-listed GPU backstop amount question was not proposed. Whether that omission is a new-topic miss depends on whether the existing library covers the topic. Two other candidates require source and independent-significance review; the actual experimental snapshot already had a Kyber topic, so its pass follows Alex's topic-level rule; whether its exact release question captures the shipping milestone remains unverified. This is not a production or full-pipeline acceptance. Details: `../hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-parallel-refinement/simple-new-question-results.zh.md`.\n109:Alex decided in D369 to capture core and supporting evidence without a strict boundary and in D370 to remove the 22 preset starting questions and separate earnings-report import. The replay entry now defaults to `poc-v118` (D374), refuses old seeded ledgers and baseline configurations, and continues to read existing non-seeded questions; earnings releases remain normal source items. This change has local contract tests but has not passed end-to-end product acceptance. The frozen historical rulers and results remain unchanged.\n245:  release, not written ([frame](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/NEW-SYSTEM-FRAME.md)).\n397:  - **Slice 1:** one owner for every upper date bound. A future date is refused, and the served product store's half-processed\n448:**The one next task: build slice 1 of the \"Forecast unavailable\" release once its build design passes council 74 (D758).** Under\n449:D439 and Alex's delegation (D750), council 73 opened release work locally at $0 (D758). Nothing is committed, published or deployed,\n462:  - the $0 release check on four stores, budgets included.\n463:- **No idea submission in the release** (council 74). The idea path reads the ledger at every step and calls a paid model; its\n470:**Earlier next task (done, D758): Alex chooses whether to open release work, and what non-number questions show (D757).** Decided by\n475:**Earlier next task (done, D757): when release work opens, a $0 check of the reader's screen for number questions (D756).** On a\n479:- **Alex closed the v13s judge line at its STOP** (D756: end the line, release with \"Forecast unavailable\"). Nothing from it enters the\n\n\ndef dependencies_of(conn, view_id):\n    \"\"\"Each dependency with its current target: the resolved view, or the waiting chain and year.\"\"\"\n    out = []\n    for dep in conn.execute('select * from dependencies where view_id=? order by dependency_id', (view_id,)):\n        dep = dict(dep)\n        resolution = conn.execute('select resolved_to, reason from dependency_resolutions where dependency_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (dep['dependency_id'],)).fetchone()\n        if resolution:\n            dep['resolved_to'], dep['resolution'] = resolution['resolved_to'], resolution['reason']\n        else:\n            dep['resolved_to'], dep['resolution'] = dep['depends_on'], ('direct' if dep['depends_on'] else 'waiting')\n        out.append(dep)\nrg: pyproject.toml: IO error for operation on pyproject.toml: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
