": true\n 44607\t },\n 44608\t \"leaks\": {\n 44609\t  \"old-3/v36@2026-08-25\": {\n 44610\t   \"latest_judgement\": 799,\n 44611\t   \"expected_judgement\": 799,\n 44612\t   \"label_kept\": true,\n 44613\t   \"answer\": \"Yes\",\n 44614\t   \"why_changed_absent\": true,\n 44615\t   \"reasons_absent\": true,\n 44616\t   \"phrase_fields\": {\n 44617\t    \"around $1 trillion\": [],\n 44618\t    \"rung 4\": [],\n 44619\t    \"at rung\": [],\n 44620\t    \"capex at rung\": []\n 44621\t   }\n 44622\t  },\n 44623\t  \"old-1/v10@2026-08-28\": {\n 44624\t   \"latest_judgement\": 865,\n 44625\t   \"expected_judgement\": 865,\n 44626\t   \"label_kept\": true,\n 44627\t   \"answer\": \"Yes\",\n 44628\t   \"why_changed_absent\": true,\n 44629\t   \"reasons_absent\": true,\n 44630\t   \"phrase_fields\": {\n 44631\t    \"around $1 trillion\": [],\n 44632\t    \"rung 4\": [],\n 44633\t    \"at rung\": [],\n 44634\t    \"capex at rung\": []\n 44635\t   }\n 44636\t  }\n 44637\t },\n 44638\t \"control\": {\n 44639\t  \"id\": \"v3\",\n 44640\t  \"answer\": \"Yes\",\n 44641\t  \"label_equals_store\": true,\n 44642\t  \"evidence_equals_store\": true\n 44643\t },\n 44644\t \"closing\": {\n 44645\t  \"reason\": \"due 2026-09-20, frozen on 2026-09-20 at rung 2 Bullish\",\n 44646\t  \"bundle_exposes_reason\": true,\n 44647\t  \"package_open\": false,\n 44648\t  \"reason_absent\": true,\n 44649\t  \"rung_label_inside_v8_fields\": [\n 44650\t   [\n 44651\t    \"questions[7].evidence[300].sources[0].title\",\n 44652\t    \"e1484\",\n 44653\t    \"Can Nvidia Reclaim $5 Trillion? Jensen Huang’s Bullish AI Call Says Yes\"\n 44654\t   ],\n 44655\t   [\n 44656\t    \"questions[7].evidence[301].sources[0].title\",\n 44657\t    \"e1485\",\n 44658\t    \"Can Nvidia Reclaim $5 Trillion? Jensen Huang’s Bullish AI Call Says Yes\"\n 44659\t   ],\n 44660\t   [\n 44661\t    \"questions[7].evidence[393].quote\",\n 44662\t    \"e1865\",\n 44663\t    \"Bullish confirmation would require firm procurement commitments for the SpaceX buildout and continued NVIDIA Data Center\"\n 44664\t   ],\n 44665\t   [\n 44666\t    \"questions[7].evidence[1167].sources[0].title\",\n 44667\t    \"e4721\",\n 44668\t    \"Oracle Surges on AI Growth as AMD, Nvidia Stay Bullish\"\n 44669\t   ],\n 44670\t   [\n 44671\t    \"questions[7].evidence[1168].sources[0].title\",\n 44672\t    \"e4722\",\n 44673\t    \"Oracle Surges on AI Growth as AMD, Nvidia Stay Bullish\"\n 44674\t   ],\n 44675\t   [\n 44676\t    \"questions[7].evidence[1169].sources[0].title\",\n 44677\t    \"e4723\",\n 44678\t    \"Oracle Surges on AI Growth as AMD, Nvidia Stay Bullish\"\n 44679\t   ]\n 44680\t  ]\n 44681\t }\n   111\t\n   112\t`src/hivemind/release.py` is the one owner, beside `service.py`.\n   113\t\n   114\t- **Constants:**\n   115\t  - `FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'`;\n   116\t  - `ALLOW_LIST = 'release-allow-list/1'`;\n   117\t  - `FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE = 'Forecast unavailable'`;\n   118\t  - `PACKAGE_FILES = {'manifest.json', 'release-data.json'}`.\n   119\t- **`ALLOWED`:** the closed key set per record type.\n   120\t\n   121\t  | Record | Keys |\n   122\t  |---|---|\n   123\t  | envelope | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `questions` |\n   124\t  | number question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (= `number`), `forecast` (= the marker), `evidence` |\n   125\t  | event or Yes/No question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (`event` or `yes_no`), `answers` (the two stored rung labels, in position order), `answer` (the stored label of the latest judgement's rung on or before the bound, or null), `evidence` |\n   126\t  | evidence in force at the bound | `id`, `one_line`, `quote`, `tier`, `speaker`, `original_who`, `original_day`, `sources` |\n   127\t  | source recorded on or before the bound | `title`, `publisher`, `day`, `uri` |\n   128\t  | manifest | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `data_sha256` |\n   129\t\n   130\t- **`question_class(views_db, view_id, labels)`** (design §3):\n   131\t  - `event` when the view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES`. The key is read as `select measure from view_keys`, and\n   132\t    only when the table exists;\n   133\t  - `yes_no` when there are exactly two labels which, through `vocabulary.canonical('label', …)`, are `Yes` and `No` in either order;\n   134\t  - `number` otherwise: a view with no key, or one whose bands cannot be resolved.\n   135\t- **`release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None)`:**\n   136\t  - pins both connections (`bundle.read_snapshot`);\n   137\t  - takes an explicit day only in canonical form: `date.fromisoformat(day).isoformat()` must equal the text given, otherwise\n   138\t    `ReleaseRefused` (so `20260825` is refused, not read as `2026-08-25`). It then resolves the bound with `service.resolve_bound`,\n   139\t    refuses a store with no default day, and uses that canonical text in every query;\n   140\t  - exports every view that exists at the bound (`service.view_exists`), closed ones included, in `created_seq, rowid` order;\n   141\t  - builds each record field by field from the table above, with column-limited SQL:\n   142\t    - `select view_id, question, created_seq from views order by created_seq, rowid`;\n   143\t    - `select position, label from rungs`;\n   144\t    - `select rung from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1`;\n   145\t    - `service.is_open_as_of`, which reads only `open` and `after_seq`;\n   146\t  - takes evidence in force from `service.evidence` and its fields from that record;\n   147\t  - looks up each source's `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri` in the items database by `input_id`. A visible source whose item is\n   148\t    missing raises `ReleaseRefused` (there is no fallback to the id);\n   149\t  - calls `check_export` on its own result before returning (AGENTS §3: the writer refuses).\n   150\t- **`check_export(data)`:** the closed-set check.\n   151\t  - Every dict at every level has exactly its record type's keys.\n   152\t  - Value checks:\n   153\t    - `format` and `allow_list` equal the constants, and `as_of` is a canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` day (`date.fromisoformat(as_of).isoformat() == as_of`);\nPython 3.10.10\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:19:def open_ledger(path):\nsrc/hivemind/bundle.py:14:def read_snapshot(*connections):\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:57:def open_db(path):\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:223:def open_read_only(path):\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:251:    failures += [] if results['old-1/v8']['same_ids_as_service_evidence'] and results['old-1/v8']['forecast'] == release.FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE else ['old-1/v8']\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_mutants.py:13:    'condition emitted on number records': (R, \"                record['forecast'] = FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE\\n            else:\\n                record['answers'] = labels\\n                record['answer'] = _answer(\",\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_mutants.py:14:                                            \"                record['forecast'] = FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE\\n                record['condition'] = 'FY2027 revenue is at least $350 billion'\\n            else:\\n                record['answers'] = labels\\n                record['answer'] = _answer(\"),\nscripts/release_build.py:1:\"\"\"Build or check the \"Forecast unavailable\" release package (docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md).\ntests/test_release.py:1:\"\"\"The \"Forecast unavailable\" release package (docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md, revision 10; D726, D758).\ntests/test_release.py:199:    assert v1['class'] == 'number' and v1['forecast'] == release.FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE\ntests/test_release.py:319:    v5.update({'class': 'number', 'forecast': release.FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE})\ntests/test_release.py:637:    assert (early['class'], early.get('forecast')) == ('number', release.FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE)\ntests/test_release.py:699:WRITER_FAULT = (\"                record['forecast'] = FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE\\n            else:\\n                record['answers'] = labels\\n                record['answer'] = _answer(\",\ntests/test_release.py:700:                \"                record['forecast'] = FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE\\n                record['condition'] = 'FY2027 revenue is at least $350 billion'\\n            else:\\n\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
