{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"agent_message","text":"**Slice 1 is not accepted.** All four saved packages matched their stores, and I found no new path in the current build that lets a forbidden or mismatched value reach a package. The remaining blockers are in verification. For example, I copied a genuine quote into the wrong question. Test 2 passed. The production checker correctly identified the wrong summary. [test_release.py:207](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:207) · [release.py:317](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:317)\n\n| Open finding | What I verified |\n|---|---|\n| **Test 2 still loses the location of a quote.** | It permits either of two fixed texts anywhere outside `v1`. I copied `v5/e6`’s “Bullish confirmation” quote into `v6/e5`’s summary. The test passed because it compares a set of texts. Round 75d required each occurrence to match its original location. [test_release.py:110](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:110) · [test_release.py:206](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:206) |\n| **Tests 11 and 21 still accept an incomplete report.** | Test 21’s assertions passed with the evidence, source and field-comparison counts omitted and `data_bytes` set to `1`. The fixture gives **5 evidence records, 6 sources, 101 comparisons and 3,313 bytes**. Both tests check the top-level keys, but neither checks all the required contents of `counts`. [test_release.py:437](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:437) · [test_release.py:614](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:614) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:241](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:241) |\n| **The acceptance script can pass the wrong release.** | In memory, changing the production marker to **“Forecast available”** made the writer, origin checker, Test 2 and final acceptance comparison agree on that wrong wording. They all read the same constant. Separately, I gave the final check an `old-2` result for June 1 with **zero questions**. It reported zero failures. For that store it checks the budgets and never checks the required default date. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:117](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:117) · [test_release.py:199](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:199) · [release_check.py:244](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:244) · [release_check.py:251](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:251) |\n| **Exact reasons are enforced for the two saved forecast refusals, but the rule still has gaps.** | Replacing the forecast used in both negative examples with `Ordinary placeholder` produced the same two exact refusals and zero acceptance failures. The script fixes the genuine analyst texts but never checks the identity of the forecast it substitutes. Test 8 also accepts a missing-item error with the evidence ID omitted, the diagnostic defect first reported in round 75. Test 10 accepts any `ValueError` containing `v5` for the class-swap case. [release_check.py:159](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:159) · [release_check.py:248](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:248) · [test_release.py:273](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:273) · [test_release.py:320](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:320) · [test_release.py:341](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:341) |\n\n**The other earlier findings are closed for the reviewed snapshots.** That includes historical classification, the ten required text fields, store paths, nonblocking pipe refusal, hashing and parsing the same bytes, ordered comparisons, staging ownership, missing-source handling, and the writer’s self-check. The mutant runner now reads the full failure text for scratch-edit errors. The three genuine examples match their fixed wording, and a stale-hash error can no longer satisfy either forecast-refusal check. [release.py:87](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:87) · [release.py:212](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:212) · [release.py:406](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:406) · [release.py:458](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:458) · [release_mutants.py:87](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_mutants.py:87) · [results.json:44567](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23e/results.json:44567)\n\n**The rewritten report’s measurements hold.** I reproduced all four comparison counts and byte sizes, both exact forecast refusals, and the 257 label-matching fields containing 32 distinct texts. The saved timings support **1.25–1.27×** the library time. The full-suite log records **425 passed**. The unsupported claims are that every acceptance assertion follows the new rule and that every missed acceptance item fails the script. The reported **31 of 32** mutant catches are a separate run, outside `results.json`. [RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:59](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:59) · [RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:93](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:93) · [results.json:44597](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23e/results.json:44597) · [full-suite output:1](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/tasks/bimnzicji.output:1)"}}
